% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `abort_handler`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no code of
% `abort_handler` is printed or held.  Step 3n (2026-11-25), for the
% held pimfep##pimos_scsi_front_end on the bridge's path
% (psi/fep_bridge.py).  Each method is INTERPOLATED (labelled) from:
%   - docs/simpos/required/classes.tsv (row `abort_handler`): sent by
%     pimfep and pimmcsp, as a simpos## class;
%   - pimfep##pimos_scsi_front_end create/6 @5d-65 (cells read
%     2026-11-25): `:create(#abort_handler, AH)`, then
%     `:set_abort_handler(FE, AH)`;
%   - docs/fep_services.md §6.7: the front end's {Id, 70} runs
%     abort_device/4, which sends `:abort(AbortHandler, pimos_abort,
%     DeviceProcess)`; the device process runs each interruptible
%     request under tag_catch/9 with the tag pimos_abort.
% Model (OURS): an abort handler has no state.  abort/3 does nothing,
% as no throw is modelled (process.esp tag_catch/9 runs its goal and
% never its abort goal).  On the bridge's path every 70 comes with
% nothing outstanding on its device (PIMOS's simpos_user_device, after
% its 620 is answered: fep_services.md §7.1 "abort, nothing
% outstanding": the FEP owes nothing), so a throw would have nothing
% to interrupt.

class abort_handler has

% INTERPOLATED from: the front end's create/6 @5d-61.
:create(Class, Handler) :- :new(Class, Handler);

instance

% INTERPOLATED from: fep_services.md §6.7 (abort_device/4's send).
% No throw is modelled: it succeeds and does nothing.
:abort(Handler, Tag, Process) ;

end.
